# Provision the Dataverse `managedidentities` record needed by Pattern A
# (plugin → Managed Identity direct call).
#
# Usage: send this request via the REST Client extension in VS Code, or
# adapt to PowerShell/curl. The request must be authenticated as a Dataverse
# user with permission to create `managedidentity` records (typically a
# system administrator).
#
# Replace placeholders:
#   <orgURL>       — e.g. https://contoso.crm.dynamics.com
#   <appId>        — UAMI clientId or App Registration appId
#   <newGuid>      — generate a fresh GUID for managedidentityid
#   <tenantId>     — Entra Directory ID

@orgURL = https://<orgURL>
@accessToken = Bearer <user token for Dataverse Web API>

POST {{orgURL}}/api/data/v9.0/managedidentities
Authorization: {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
OData-MaxVersion: 4.0
OData-Version: 4.0
Accept: application/json

{
  "applicationid": "<appId>",
  "managedidentityid": "<newGuid>",
  "credentialsource": 2,
  "subjectscope": 1,
  "tenantid": "<tenantId>",
  "version": 1
}

###
# After creating the record, link the assembly to the managed identity. This
# is normally done via the Plugin Identity Manager XrmToolBox tool. The
# corresponding Federated Identity Credential on the Entra app must use
# subject:
#   component:pluginassembly,thumbprint:<assembly thumbprint>,environment:<environment id>
# and issuer:
#   https://<env-prefix>.<env-suffix>.environment.api.powerplatform.com/sts
